-- Forty additional media interview dialogues on technology, industry economics, wellbeing and fandom.
WITH seed(category,media_types,question_text,a,b,c,d) AS (VALUES
('recording_technology',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you ever use AI-generated ideas during songwriting?','I''d treat them as prompts and still write the music ourselves.','We''d check originality, permissions and how they fit the song.','Technology shouldn''t stop us from making something genuinely new.','I''ll listen, but it still has to survive the band''s veto.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What would make you reject an AI-generated vocal or instrumental track?','If it replaced the expression of a real performer without consent.','We''d consider rights, quality and what the listeners expect.','If it can''t carry real emotion, it has no place in our music.','If the robot insists on a forty-minute solo, it''s out.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How important is it that a finished track lasts a certain length?','The song should be as long as its story needs.','I''d avoid padding but make sure the arrangement feels complete.','A great idea deserves room to develop, not an arbitrary cutoff.','I''d rather hear ninety great seconds than six minutes of noodling.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What do you do when a recording session repeatedly fails?','We stay patient and work out what''s going wrong.','I''d check the technical process before booking more time.','If the system fails, we find another way to capture the song.','The band gets tea while the engineer fights the computer.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Do you prefer natural room sound or tightly edited production?','I love hearing musicians play together in a real space.','We choose the method that best supports each song.','A raw recording with character can beat sterile perfection.','If you can hear my chair squeak, maybe turn that down.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Could a virtual studio ever replace recording in the same room?','Remote sessions make collaboration possible across distances.','We''d use remote tools but protect the connection between players.','Nothing completely replaces the moment everyone locks into a groove.','A video call can''t tell me who stole my guitar pick.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'How do you keep a new recording exciting after hearing it a hundred times?','I take listening breaks and return with fresh ears.','We test it with trusted people who haven''t heard the demos.','If the energy disappears, we''ll change the arrangement.','I ban the chorus from the van speakers for a week.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you share your unfinished recordings with a producer overseas?','Yes, new perspectives can help us hear possibilities.','Only with clear agreements on access and ownership.','I''d invite a producer who challenges our whole sound.','First, I''d double-check which folder contains the embarrassing demos.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Does a perfect digital performance always sound better than a human one?','No, tiny imperfections can make a take feel alive.','We fix distractions while keeping the character of the player.','A real performance should have a pulse, not just perfect timing.','Our drummer would like this question removed from the transcript.'),
('recording_technology',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What should musicians understand before licensing a recording to a platform?','They should know who owns the work and how payments flow.','I''d read the rights, territory and revenue terms carefully.','Artists deserve real control over where their songs appear.','I refuse to sign anything printed in microscopic lettering.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'When should a band negotiate better terms with its record label?','When we can demonstrate value and understand the alternatives.','We''d review our contract before starting the conversation.','I''d rather walk away than accept terms that bury the next album.','Ideally before the label sends another expensive fruit basket.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Is it realistic for a band to make a living from physical records?','It can work as part of a wider connection with fans.','We''d combine physical sales with touring and other income.','A brilliant record with loyal listeners can create its own economy.','I''d be delighted if every vinyl sale covered one meal.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you lower ticket prices if merchandise sales were strong?','I''d love to make shows accessible when we can afford it.','We''d examine the full budget instead of guessing.','More fans in the room can matter more than a bigger margin.','Let the shirt sales pay for another encore.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How would you respond if a sponsor demanded control over your lyrics?','I''d protect the meaning of our songs.','We''d set creative boundaries clearly in the agreement.','No company gets to rewrite the chorus for its slogan.','They can sponsor the cables, not the words.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What matters more when choosing a manager: contacts or trust?','Trust is the foundation for any long relationship.','A good manager needs integrity, experience and a useful network.','I''d take an honest newcomer over someone with famous phone numbers.','I want someone who returns calls and reads the contracts.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Could a band''s own merchandise company become a serious business?','Yes, if it gives fans well-made things they actually want.','We''d need reliable manufacturing, fulfilment and fair prices.','I''d love to create designs that fans wear beyond our shows.','I just don''t want to become a full-time T-shirt accountant.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should streaming services reveal more about how royalties are calculated?','Absolutely, musicians deserve to understand their earnings.','Transparent reports would help artists make better decisions.','The industry shouldn''t hide behind formulas nobody can explain.','I''d settle for a statement that fits on one screen.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['radio','podcast','tv']::text[],'Would a large recording advance change your musical ambitions?','I''d still want to make the songs we believe in.','We''d invest cautiously instead of treating an advance as profit.','I''d use the opportunity to build our most ambitious record yet.','First I''d buy the drummer a chair that doesn''t wobble.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How should small venues survive when major tours dominate ticket sales?','They need loyal communities and a pipeline of local talent.','Sensible costs and consistent bookings matter as much as publicity.','The biggest artists should remember where their careers began.','I''d happily play a club with enough sockets for our amps.'),
('music_economy',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you release music independently even if it meant slower growth?','Yes, if it meant keeping control of what we create.','We''d compare the long-term costs and benefits.','I''d rather build something we own than chase an easy headline.','Ask me again when I''m packing the thousandth CD.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How do you protect your voice during a long run of concerts?','I warm up, rest when I can and take warning signs seriously.','We build sensible breaks into a busy schedule.','No encore is worth risking the next month''s shows.','I try not to shout over the bassist at breakfast.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Can an artist become too focused on chasing fame?','Yes, success means little if you lose everyone close to you.','We need goals that include health and creative satisfaction.','The moment charts own your life, something''s gone wrong.','My family reminds me the kitchen doesn''t care about fame.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'How do you recover after an exhausting international tour?','I reconnect with the people and routines I''ve missed.','Rest, recovery and a gradual return to rehearsal help.','A proper break gives me ideas I''d never find on the road.','I sleep until the suitcase stops following me.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should managers be allowed to push artists into endless bookings?','Nobody should sacrifice their health just to fill a calendar.','We need clear limits and honest conversations about workload.','I''d rather turn down a lucrative date than lose the whole band.','If the calendar needs three colours of warning, it''s too full.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'What happens when one band member needs time away for personal reasons?','We support them and find a plan that respects their privacy.','We''d revisit the schedule together and avoid rushing decisions.','A band should be strong enough to put people before publicity.','The tour can wait; friendship can''t always.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Does creative burnout affect the quality of music?','It can make every new idea feel like hard work.','We watch for fatigue and adjust expectations early.','Pushing harder isn''t always the answer; sometimes you need silence.','That''s when I start thinking the metronome is judging me.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['radio','podcast','tv']::text[],'Do you find it difficult to switch off after a huge live show?','Adrenaline lasts long after the audience has left.','A quiet routine helps me wind down before sleep.','Sometimes the energy is so strong I want to write another song.','My brain is still playing the encore at three in the morning.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How do you keep disagreements from damaging friendships in a band?','We try to address the issue without attacking the person.','Cooling off before difficult conversations makes a difference.','I''ll argue fiercely for a song, then make peace afterwards.','We have a rule against discussing mixes while hungry.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you postpone an album if the band wasn''t ready emotionally?','Yes, the music will be better if everyone is well.','We''d communicate a realistic new plan to everyone involved.','A delayed honest record beats a rushed, miserable one.','The album can wait until we''ve all remembered how to sleep.'),
('career_wellbeing',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should the music industry talk more openly about performers'' mental health?','Yes, honest conversations can make people feel less isolated.','Better support and realistic schedules matter more than slogans.','Success shouldn''t require anyone to pretend they''re invincible.','I''d like fewer motivational posters and more actual help.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Do viral social-media moments translate into ticket sales?','Sometimes, but people need a reason to stay interested.','We watch whether online attention turns into real engagement.','A great live clip can make someone travel to see the full show.','A million views still can''t fit in one tiny venue.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'What would make you respond personally to a fan''s message?','A sincere story about what one of our songs meant to them.','I read as many as I can without pretending I can answer all.','A thoughtful question is always worth my attention.','Anyone who sends a photo of a truly bizarre band T-shirt.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you let fans vote on the design of a new tour poster?','Their ideas could give the design a new perspective.','We''d offer a few strong options and credit the designer.','I''d pick the wildest proposal that still suits the music.','Only if they don''t put a cartoon potato in our logo.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How do you tell the difference between criticism and online harassment?','Criticism discusses the work; harassment targets people.','We set clear rules for behaviour across our pages.','Nobody has to tolerate threats to prove they''re open to feedback.','Disliking a riff is fine; chasing us around the internet isn''t.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'Would you perform an unreleased song live for a fan gathering?','Yes, sharing a work in progress can be special.','We''d pick something we''re comfortable showing before release.','A small audience is the perfect place for a risky new idea.','Just remember the lyrics aren''t finished yet.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Should bands use their own avatars and images in social posts?','Personal visuals help fans recognise who''s speaking.','We''d make sure the imagery reflects the real band identity.','I''d rather see our faces than another anonymous publicity graphic.','As long as nobody stretches my head into a guitar pick.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How do you feel about fans remixing clips of your performances?','It''s exciting when people respond creatively to the music.','We''d encourage responsible sharing while respecting rights.','Sometimes fans make more imaginative edits than our team.','I just hope they don''t loop my worst missed note.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Can an online fan community become as meaningful as a local music scene?','Yes, people can build genuine friendships around music.','Online connection works best when people feel safe and included.','A worldwide community could become its own musical movement.','I''d still love everyone to meet at a proper gig.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'What would you do if a fake account claimed to speak for your band?','We''d warn fans and clarify which channels are official.','We''d report impersonation and avoid sharing sensitive details.','A fake account won''t get to rewrite our story.','If they promise free tour buses, it''s definitely not me.'),
('fans_social',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How do you thank people who share your songs with friends?','Their word of mouth means more than they might realise.','We try to acknowledge supporters and keep releasing good music.','A recommendation from a real fan can beat a huge advert.','Tell them they''ve earned a very enthusiastic high five.')
), inserted AS (
INSERT INTO public.interview_questions
(category,media_types,question_text,option_a_text,option_a_effects,option_b_text,option_b_effects,option_c_text,option_c_effects,option_d_text,option_d_effects)
SELECT s.category,s.media_types,s.question_text,
s.a,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.03,'fan_mult',1.04,'cash_mult',1.00,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('authentic',2,'professional',1)),
s.b,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.01,'fan_mult',1.02,'cash_mult',1.02,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('diplomatic',2,'professional',2)),
s.c,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.05,'fan_mult',0.99,'cash_mult',0.99,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('bold',2,'rebellious',2)),
s.d,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.02,'fan_mult',1.01,'cash_mult',1.00,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('unpredictable',2,'authentic',1))
FROM seed s WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.interview_questions q WHERE lower(btrim(q.question_text))=lower(btrim(s.question_text)))
RETURNING id
) SELECT count(*)::integer AS inserted_count FROM inserted;